y, &amp;quotEdward, you are smart,&amp;quot but then she would say, &amp;quotBut not enough.&amp;quot  Truth be told, there were a number of occasions of late where she proved to be right, but we\'re talking here about art, not my personal life---aren\'t we?\\r\\n&lt;br&gt;</itunes:summary>\\r\\n    </item>\\r\\n    <item>\\r\\n      <title>Does Tim Hawkinson Have Multiple Personalities?</title>\\r\\n      <link>http://kcrw.com/cgi-bin/db/kcrw.pl?show_code=at&amp;air_date=07/05/05&amp;tmplt_type=Show</link>\\r\\n      <itunes:author xmlns:itunes=\\"http://www.itunes.com/DTDs/Podcast-1.0.dtd\\">Edward Goldman</itunes:author>\\r\\n      <itunes:subtitle xmlns:itunes=\\"http://www.itunes.com/DTDs/Podcast-1.0.dtd\\">The opening of Tim Hawkinson\'s exhibition at LACMA a couple of weeks ago turned into an event memorable not only as a chance to celebrate the work of one of the most inventive artists working today, but also an occasion to observe a crowd behaving in a most unusual way: with goofy smiles on their faces, adult men and women were giggling or intently staring in total disbelief.   And let me admit for the record that, as for myself, I was guilty on both counts.\\r\\n&lt;br&gt;</itunes:subtitle>\\r\\n      <itunes:summary xmlns:itunes=\\"http://www.itunes.com/DTDs/Podcast-1.0.dtd\\">The opening of Tim Hawkinson\'s exhibition at LACMA a couple of weeks ago turned into an event memorable not only as a chance to celebrate the work of one of the most inventive artists working today, but also an occasion to observe a crowd behaving in a most unusual way: with goofy smiles on their faces, adult men and women were giggling or intently staring in total disbelief.   And let me admit for the record that, as for myself, I was guilty on both counts.\\r\\n&lt;br&gt;</itunes:summary>\\r\\n      <itunes:category xmlns:itunes=\\"http://www.itunes.com/DTDs/Podcast-1.0.dtd\\">\\r\\n        <itunes:category text=\\"Arts &amp; Entertainment\\" />\\r\\n      </itunes:category>\\r\\